 - Added shared Mapscript-related world-size helpers. Note: done in [SAS_WorldSizeUtils.py](/Assets/Python/SAS_WorldSizeUtils.py) rather than in the [PrivateMaps](/PrivateMaps/) folder as a .py file. This is because such a previous design caused the helper-as-a-playable-mapscript related bug, in AdvCiv-SAS only, of RandomScriptMap and Archipelago, e.g. at Huge world size, being generated far too small (`60 x 44`). After the fix it returned to `120 x 84`, matching base AdvCiv visually at a glance, and not being overly cramped anymore. The same issue may also have affected other map scripts that imported the old helper. The old helper now only keeps the minimal new playable mapscript code, not imported by other mapscripts anymore, in the new **SAS_Simple_Flat_Grass**: a simple sandbox map with almost all land and mostly flat grass tiles. See [SAS_Simple_Flat_Grass.py](/PrivateMaps/SAS_Simple_Flat_Grass.py).
-- Tuned several inherited map scripts: [RandomScriptMap.py](/PrivateMaps/RandomScriptMap.py) is trimmed slightly; [Medium_and_Small.py](/PrivateMaps/Medium_and_Small.py) is enlarged a little from Large onward because lower islets usually are not assigned to players, leaving the upper continent-style area cramped; [Big_and_Small.py](/PrivateMaps/Big_and_Small.py) and [Custom_Continents.py](/PrivateMaps/Custom_Continents.py) are trimmed on larger tiers because Huge tested too large.
+- Tuned several inherited map scripts: [RandomScriptMap.py](/PrivateMaps/RandomScriptMap.py) is trimmed slightly; [Medium_and_Small.py](/PrivateMaps/Medium_and_Small.py) is enlarged a little from Large onward because lower islets usually are not assigned to players, leaving the upper continent-style area cramped; [Big_and_Small.py](/PrivateMaps/Big_and_Small.py), [Custom_Continents.py](/PrivateMaps/Custom_Continents.py), and [Donut.py](/PrivateMaps/Donut.py) are trimmed on larger tiers because Huge tested too large.
 - **Reduced the grid size** of some maps that are **almost entirely composed of land** plots: city spacing **was too wide** due to the **excess of land** and **lack of water** plots. See [SAS_WorldSizeUtils.py](/Assets/Python/SAS_WorldSizeUtils.py).
 - **Earth2 start distribution rework:** for Huge and beyond world sizes, keep Earth2 at its existing **Huge-scale sizing** (already large enough), but solve crowding by **populating underused landmasses instead** (e.g., min 16 players before Africa is populated, min 32 players before the whole world is populated) of enlarging the script further. **Thresholds are based on player count** (not world size). See [`GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml`](/Assets/XML/GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml).
 - **Reduce grid size** for each worldsize in [Global_Highlands.py](/PrivateMaps/Global_Highlands.py) by one world size (e.g. World Size Huge was `(38,24)` -> `(32,20)` (old World Size Large's dimensions)): empirically even accounting for the many peaks it has (compensated by a larger grid at each world size than usual), **cities were still too sparse**. See [KI#138](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#138---fixed-base-advciv-issue-global-highlands-map-sizes-were-too-large).

